		<unit label="chapter" identifier="1" level="3">Creation and Limitation of Estates</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="4">Rule Against Perpetuities</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>55.1-129</section_number>
	<catch_line>Uniformity of application and construction</catch_line>
	<text>
		Sections 55.1-124 through 55.1-129 shall be applied and construed to effectuate their general purpose to make the law uniform with respect to the rule against perpetuities among states enacting it.
	</text>
	<history>2000, c. 714, § 55-12.6; 2019, c. 712.</history>
